  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_pat",
  "prompt": "For each price change that took effect from 1 to 28 February 2025, label it and compare the units before and after it. A price change is a version in price_history whose list_price_eur differs from that of the product's version before it, dated by its valid_from: a rise when the new price is higher, a cut when it is lower. Its change week is the week (Monday to Sunday) that holds valid_from. The before window is the 8 weeks just before the change week and the after window the 8 weeks just after it; the change week itself is in neither. Units come from weekly_units, which has a row for every product and week (week_start is the Monday), with 0 for a week with no sale. A product launched during a window keeps its change, with 0 units in its weeks before the launch. Return five columns, in this order: product_id, valid_from, change_type ('rise' or 'cut'), units_before (the units over the before window) and units_after (over the after window). Return one row for each price change. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "product_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "valid_from",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "change_type",
        "type_class": "text"
